---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, LEGAL_EFFECTIVE_DATE, SITE_DOMAIN } from '../lib/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="The terms that govern your use of NetWageTax's free tax and paycheck calculators, including fair use, disclaimers of warranty, and limitation of liability."
>
  <div class="border-b border-slate-200 bg-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 sm:py-16">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-slate-900 sm:text-4xl">Terms of Use</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-slate-500">Effective and last updated: {LEGAL_EFFECTIVE_DATE}</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <article class="prose-page mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6">
    <p>
      These Terms of Use (“Terms”) govern your access to and use of {SITE_DOMAIN} and the calculators, content, and
      features offered on it (together, the “Service”), operated by NetWageTax (“NetWageTax,” “we,” “us,” or “our”).
      By accessing or using the Service, you agree to be bound by these Terms and by our
      <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>. If you do not agree, do not use the Service.
    </p>

    <h2 id="service">1. The Service</h2>
    <p>
      NetWageTax provides free, browser-based calculators and explanatory content about U.S. payroll and income tax
      topics. The Service is provided for general informational and educational purposes only. We may add, change,
      suspend, or discontinue any part of the Service at any time without notice or liability.
    </p>

    <h2 id="eligibility">2. Eligibility</h2>
    <p>
      You must be at least 13 years old to use the Service. If you use the Service on behalf of an organization, you
      represent that you are authorized to accept these Terms on its behalf.
    </p>

    <h2 id="not-advice">3. Not tax, legal, or financial advice</h2>
    <p>
      The Service does not provide tax, legal, accounting, or financial advice, and no professional-client
      relationship is created by your use of it. Results are estimates based on the information you enter and our
      interpretation of published law and guidance, which may change. You are solely responsible for the accuracy of
      your tax returns and for any decisions you make. Please read our full
      <a href="/disclaimer">Financial &amp; Tax Disclaimer</a>, which forms part of these Terms.
    </p>

    <h2 id="fair-use">4. Acceptable and fair use</h2>
    <p>
      You may use the Service for your personal, non-commercial purposes, and professionals may use it as a reference
      in their own work. You agree not to:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Use the Service in violation of any applicable law or regulation</li>
      <li>
        Scrape, crawl, or harvest content or results through automated means at a volume that burdens the Service,
        except for search engines indexing public pages in accordance with our robots directives
      </li>
      <li>Attempt to interfere with, disrupt, overload, or gain unauthorized access to the Service or its infrastructure</li>
      <li>Introduce malware, or probe, scan, or test the vulnerability of the Service without our written permission</li>
      <li>
        Frame, mirror, or republish the Service or substantial portions of its content as your own, or present it in a
        way that suggests our endorsement
      </li>
      <li>
        Generate invalid advertising impressions or clicks, or otherwise interfere with the advertising that supports
        the Service
      </li>
      <li>Misrepresent the Service’s output as professional advice or as an official IRS determination</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Brief quotations with attribution and a link back to the Service are welcome.
    </p>

    <h2 id="ip">5. Intellectual property</h2>
    <p>
      The Service, including its text, design, graphics, code, and the selection and arrangement of its content, is
      owned by NetWageTax or its licensors and is protected by U.S. and international copyright, trademark, and other
      laws. Subject to these Terms, we grant you a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable license to access
      and use the Service. All rights not expressly granted are reserved. Statutory text and official IRS materials
      referenced on the Site remain in the public domain.
    </p>

    <h2 id="third-party">6. Third-party content, links, and advertising</h2>
    <p>
      The Service may display advertisements and link to third-party websites. We do not control and are not
      responsible for third-party content, products, services, or privacy practices, and a link or advertisement does
      not constitute an endorsement. Your dealings with advertisers are solely between you and them.
    </p>

    <h2 id="warranty">7. Disclaimer of warranties</h2>
    <p class="uppercase text-sm tracking-wide">
      The Service is provided “as is” and “as available,” without warranties of any kind, whether express, implied, or
      statutory, including implied warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, title,
      non-infringement, and accuracy. We do not warrant that the Service will be uninterrupted, error-free, secure, or
      current, or that any calculation, estimate, or content is accurate or complete.
    </p>

    <h2 id="liability">8. Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p class="uppercase text-sm tracking-wide">
      To the fullest extent permitted by law, NetWageTax and its owners, operators, contributors, and service
      providers will not be liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential, exemplary, or punitive
      damages, or for any taxes, penalties, interest, lost profits, or lost data, arising out of or related to your use
      of, or inability to use, the Service, even if advised of the possibility of such damages. Because the Service is
      free, our total liability for any claim arising out of or relating to the Service will not exceed one hundred
      U.S. dollars (US$100).
    </p>
    <p>
      Some jurisdictions do not allow the exclusion of certain warranties or the limitation of certain damages, so
      some of the above may not apply to you.
    </p>

    <h2 id="indemnity">9. Indemnification</h2>
    <p>
      You agree to indemnify and hold harmless NetWageTax and its owners and operators from any claims, losses,
      liabilities, and expenses (including reasonable attorneys’ fees) arising from your violation of these Terms or
      your misuse of the Service.
    </p>

    <h2 id="law">10. Governing law</h2>
    <p>
      These Terms are governed by the laws of the United States and the laws of the state in which NetWageTax is
      organized, without regard to conflict-of-law principles. Any dispute arising under these Terms will be resolved
      exclusively in the state or federal courts located in that state, and you consent to their personal
      jurisdiction.
    </p>

    <h2 id="general">11. General</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Changes.</strong> We may revise these Terms at any time by posting an updated version and changing the
        “last updated” date. Continued use of the Service after changes take effect constitutes acceptance.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Severability.</strong> If any provision is found unenforceable, the remaining provisions remain in full
        force and effect.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>No waiver.</strong> Our failure to enforce any right or provision is not a waiver of that right or
        provision.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Entire agreement.</strong> These Terms, together with our Privacy Policy and Disclaimer, are the entire
        agreement between you and NetWageTax regarding the Service.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="contact">12. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about these Terms can be sent to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
